## Database Safety Rules

1. Never run migrations without confirmation. Always run `alembic current`
   before generating or upgrading.
2. Always verify `SELECT current_database() = 'cip'` before any DB-affecting
   command.
3. Never use `git add -A` or `git add .` — explicit path staging only.
4. Tests must not write to `cip` unless `ALLOW_TESTS_ON_DEV_DB=1` is set.
5. Do not run `alembic upgrade` against production without explicit instruction.
6. Wipe scripts destroy all application data — use only in dev/demo contexts.
7. Seed scripts with default args run destructive demo seed. Use
   `--commercial-system-reference-only` to insert only reference dimensions.
8. Before generating a new migration, always run `alembic current` to confirm
   the current head and set `down_revision` correctly.

