## Known Gotchas

| Issue | Context | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| `numpy.bool_` in PM upsert | Product Master commit produces numpy scalars that SQLAlchemy rejects | Cast to Python native `bool()` before persistence |
| `MissingGreenlet` from lazy loads | Accessing relationships in async endpoints without eager loading raises `MissingGreenlet` | Always use `joinedload()` or `selectinload()` for relationships in async context |
| Circular import — DSI corroboration | `dsi_shipment_corroboration.py` imports from `distributor_sales_inventory.py` which imports from it | Use lazy imports inside function bodies in `dsi_shipment_corroboration.py` |
| `seed.py` syntax error on line 43 | Known issue in the seed script | Fix or bypass as needed |
| ESLint 9 flat config | Next.js ESLint integration requires env var | Set `ESLINT_USE_FLAT_CONFIG=false` before running lint |
| API tests need dev DB flag | Pytest suite refuses to run against `cip` without opt-in | Set `ALLOW_TESTS_ON_DEV_DB=1` in test environment |
| Port preflight check | `dev-api.js` checks for stale processes on :8001 | Set `CIP_SKIP_API_PORT_PREFLIGHT=1` to bypass |
| Python 3.13+ incompatible | `asyncpg` may not build on Python 3.13+ | Use Python 3.12.x |
| str_dim_flags not flattened | Tuple arguments not flattened in PM bulk upsert SQL | Flatten before passing to SQL parameters |
| `alembic upgrade` on wrong DB | Running migration against wrong database | Always verify `current_database()` first |
| DSI eligibility before corroboration | Inactive candidates filtered before corroboration runs so cross-distributor fallback has no candidates to intersect | Apply historical eligibility relaxation before building the eligible candidate set passed to corroboration |
| psycopg3 typeless NULLs in VALUES clause | Python `None` is sent as a typeless NULL by psycopg3. PostgreSQL defaults untyped NULLs to `text`. CASE expressions mixing a VALUES clause column with an ORM model column fail with `DatatypeMismatch` if the ORM column is non-text (Integer, Date, etc.) | Wrap non-text VALUES staging columns in `cast(col, Type)` inside any CASE/SELECT that mixes them with ORM columns. String columns are unaffected — PostgreSQL defaults to text which matches varchar. |

