## Git Workflow

1. Explicit path staging only — never `git add -A` or `git add .`
2. Never commit: `.env`, database dumps, log files, `.specstory`,
   `.cursor/rules` changes without approval
3. Always work on a feature branch — never push directly to `main`
4. Never push to `main` without explicit instruction ("promote to main"
   or "merge to main") — main promotion is always a separate delivery task
5. Commit messages: descriptive, prefixed with module name
   (e.g., `dsi: fix cross-distributor corroboration fallback`)
6. Before pushing: run `pnpm lint` and `pnpm test:web` at minimum
7. A committed unit must work from a fresh checkout — no uncommitted
   dependencies allowed

